<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span><span id="A1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Formulas and Principles for Comparison Methods</span></h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Data Contamination Detection</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the output of the model’s greedy decoding as <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>. Below are the definitions of several contamination detection methods.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Perplexity</span>: calculates the perplexity of the response generated by the model through greedy decoding, as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{Perplexity}=\exp\left(-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\log P(y_{i})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Perplexity</mtext><mo>=</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mi>log</mi><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Perplexity}=\exp\left(-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\log P(y_{i})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where N is the length of the greedy decoded output, <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>.
Lower perplexity indicates higher contamination levels.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mink% Prob</span>: Computes the negative average log probability of the k% least
probable tokens in the response generated by the model through greedy decoding, as:</p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{Min-k}(y)=-\frac{1}{E}\sum_{y_{i}\in\text{Min-k\%(y)}}\log P(y_{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Min-k</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>E</mi></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mtext>Min-k%(y)</mtext></mrow></munder><mi>log</mi><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Min-k}(y)=-\frac{1}{E}\sum_{y_{i}\in\text{Min-k\%(y)}}\log P(y_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where E is the size of the Min-K%(y) set, and Min-K%(y) is the set of k% least probable tokens in the response. Smaller values of Min-k% Prob indicate higher contamination levels.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Contamination Mitigation Evaluation</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">TED: filters non-memorized samples through multiple sampling rounds, using these samples
for contamination mitigation evaluation. It is illustrated as:</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{e}=\left\{s\mid s\in S\wedge\mathrm{EditDist}\left(s,s^{\text{greedy}}\right)&gt;\tau\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>s</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mi>EditDist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mtext>greedy</mtext></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{e}=\left\{s\mid s\in S\wedge\mathrm{EditDist}\left(s,s^{\text{greedy}}\right)&gt;\tau\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of outputs sampled from LLM, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\text{greedy}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mtext>greedy</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\text{greedy}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the output generated by the LLM using greedy decoding, and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is a predefined threshold for the edit distance. The set <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> contains only those samples from <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> for which the edit distance to the greedy decoding output exceeds the threshold <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Contamination Mitigation Evaluation on the Summarization Task</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To achieve a broader validation of the effectiveness of LNE-Blocking across benchmarks, we conducted experiments on a summarization task using the ACLSum <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Takeshita et al., 2024</a>)</cite> dataset. This dataset, released in 2024, is specifically designed for aspect-based summarization of scientific publications. The models evaluated were Qwen2.5-7B and Qwen2.5-14B, and we employed the ROUGE-L metric to measure the similarity between model-generated outputs and the reference summaries. The <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Threshold\_Task" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Threshold\_Task</annotation></semantics></math> was set to 30, and both contamination simulation and inference were conducted using a two-shot prompt.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Contamination mitigation evaluation on Summarization, where values outside the parentheses represent model performance, ROUGE-L, while those inside the parentheses represent the PG
metric based on ROUGE-L.</figcaption>
